k 1)\\n4: \\n5: Scan of Task 1 text against itself and the plan's Global Constraints — a table, not a verdict.\\n6: \\n7: | Pair / self-consistency | What one produces vs what the other consumes | Finding |\\n8: |---|---|---|\\n9: | Task 1 code spec (`greeting.js` returns `\\\"Hello, \\\" + name.trim() + \\\"!\\\"`) vs Task 1 tests | test asserts `greet('Ada')==='Hello, Ada!'`, `greet('  Ada  ')==='Hello, Ada!'`, `greet('')==='Hello, !'`, `greet('   ')==='Hello, !'` | consistent: trim() makes all four hold |\\n10: | Task 1 interfaces (produces string, no type guard) vs PRD Out (no runtime type guard) | both say no non-string handling | consistent |\\n11: | Task 1 file paths vs repo reality | brief/plan text sometimes says `src/greeting.js`/`test/greeting.test.js`; repo has root `greeting.js`/`greeting.test.js` | path mismatch — implementer must use root paths |\\n12: | Task 1 `test('normal greeting', ...)` must stay unchanged vs Step 1 \\\"append after line 4\\\" | normal test is line 4, append 3 after it | consistent |\\n13: | Global Constraint \\\"branch name `feat/REAL-001-trim-surrounding-whitespace`\\\" vs actual branch `feat/REAL-001-greeting` | branch name differs from plan | ruling: continue on existing feature branch (not main/master); flag mismatch as concern |\\n14: | Global Constraint \\\"MR via glab\\\" vs `git remote -v` empty | no remote configured | ruling: skip MR, record as concern |\\n15: \\n16: ## Rulings\\n17: \\n18: - **R1 (branch name mismatch)**: Plan Global Constraints name the branch `feat/REAL-001-trim-surrounding-whitespace`, but the working tree is already on `feat/REAL-001-greeting` (contains the initial fixture + prototype). This is not a destructive op and the branch is not main/master. Ruling: continue implementing on the existing `feat/REAL-001-greeting` branch; record the name mismatch as a concern for the human. Cost if wrong: branch-name drift, but no functional impact (code paths are root-level regardless).\\n19: - **R2 (no remo